From: CroqueMr <82093548+CroqueMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:59:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/44] avutil/dovi_meta: add a trailer for original RPU
 extension block bytes

Add fields to AVDOVIDmData that let a decoder retain the original,
bit-packed bytes of a Dolby Vision RPU extension block alongside the
parsed values, for CB1's native Dolby Vision bridge. A magic value marks
the trailer as present even when the block value is zero.

From libreelec-x86-DV R1.0.0-Beta4 (f0f947a), CB1/patches/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-9900-02-libavutil__dovi_meta.h.patch
https://github.com/CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV
---
 libavutil/dovi_meta.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/dovi_meta.h b/libavutil/dovi_meta.h
index c102bf384f..598d2440f1 100644
--- a/libavutil/dovi_meta.h
+++ b/libavutil/dovi_meta.h
@@ -332,6 +332,11 @@ typedef struct AVDOVIDmData {
         AVDOVIDmLevel254 l254; /* static */
         AVDOVIDmLevel255 l255; /* static */
     };
+    /* Dvbridge isolated-lab trailer. Preserve presence even when value is zero.
+     * Original RPU block bytes are bit-packed, NOT HDMI payload bytes. */
+    uint32_t dvbridge_raw_magic;
+    uint32_t dvbridge_original_length;
+    uint8_t dvbridge_original_bytes[32];
 } AVDOVIDmData;
 
